# Bundly — line-ending normalization
#
# WHY: without this, editors on Windows save with CRLF and editors on
# Linux/Mac save with LF, and `git diff` shows every text file as
# "modified" with thousands of lines changed even when no real edit was
# made. That noise hides real diffs and makes review impossible.
#
# WHAT: `* text=auto` tells git to detect text files automatically and
# store them with LF in the index (repo). On checkout, Windows users
# still get CRLF in their working tree (git converts on the way out),
# Linux/Mac users get LF — but the canonical form in the repo is LF.
# This is what production (Render = Linux) actually reads.
#
# HOW TO ADOPT (one-time): after committing this file, run
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "chore: normalize line endings to LF"
# That re-stages every text file with the canonical EOL.

* text=auto

# Binary files — never normalize, never diff as text
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.svg    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.xls    binary
*.zip    binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.mp4    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.db     binary
*.sqlite binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts (bash on Linux
# breaks on \r\n shebangs).
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Render expects LF for these (parsed by Linux YAML / shell tools).
render.yaml          text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml     text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yaml    text eol=lf
